digraph Accessors { graph [layout=twopi,label="When should accessor methods be used?",labelloc=t,fontsize=22]; node [shape=box,style=rounded]; Main [label="Accessor & Mutator Design",shape=ellipse]; Good [label="Use getters when read access is necessary"]; Enc [label="Preserve encapsulation"]; Set [label="Use setters only when mutation is permitted"]; Risk [label="Avoid exposing internal representation"]; Law [label="Prefer domain operations over arbitrary setters"]; Tests [label="Validate changes and preserve invariants"]; Main -> {Good Enc Set Risk Law Tests}; Good -> "Needed for display/reporting"; Enc -> "Private fields"; Set -> "Check allowed states"; Risk -> "Return copies of mutable data"; Law -> "e.g. addToCart() not setItems()"; Tests -> "Immutable DVD fields after creation"; }